4
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:06,580
What did you feel

5
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,660
when you were close to her?

6
00:00:08,680 --> 00:00:09,800
I wanted to stop,

7
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:11,400
but I couldn't.

8
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:13,140
I couldn't stop myself.

9
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:15,860
I know your body is rejecting this...

10
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:18,840
I'll make you want to hug me.

11
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,760
I was in a car accident several years ago.

12
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,340
My doctor said the accident made me

13
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:24,200
reject physical contact.

14
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,060
What did you feel

15
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,240
when you were close to her?

16
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:32,840
I wanted to stop,

17
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:34,840
but I couldn't.

18
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:37,480
I couldn't stop myself.

19
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:39,600
This is your life.

20
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:42,800
Are you going to let guilt
stop you from being happy?

21
00:00:43,480 --> 00:00:45,840
If someone who saved me isn't happy,

22
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:47,720
then how could I be happy?

23
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,480
I'm sorry.

24
00:00:52,920 --> 00:00:54,160
I can't do this.

25
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:06,080
I have a girlfriend.

26
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:20,680
[Third Person]

27
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:32,800
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

28
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:37,920
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

29
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:41,820
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

30
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:48,100
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

31
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:57,820
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

32
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:02,880
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

33
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:07,180
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

34
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:15,840
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

35
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:25,000
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

36
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:41,760
I had been dating
my girlfriend for a long time

37
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,240
until an accident happened four years ago.

38
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:50,520
I lost my memories.

39
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:53,680
I forgot everything,

40
00:02:57,740 --> 00:02:59,440
including my girlfriend.

41
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,700
She always took care of me,

42
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:06,500
but my memories never returned.

43
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:10,320
I can't remember the love I had for her,

44
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,560
and we always argued.

45
00:03:17,900 --> 00:03:19,900
I actually asked to break up,

46
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:25,320
but her parents pressured me.

47
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,680
So I had to stay with her.

48
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:31,720
It sounds like an excuse,

49
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:37,400
but it's the truth.

50
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:40,400
Things are complicated.

51
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:44,520
It feels like it's over, but it isn't.

52
00:03:45,580 --> 00:03:47,820
And I don't know when it will actually end.

53
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,780
So you want to stop
what happens between us?

54
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,980
I'm so sorry.

55
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,680
I don't want to wrong
you and her any further.

56
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:12,220
I don't want you to be
in this terrible relationship.

57
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:17,520
Someone sweet like you
deserves good love.

58
00:04:18,800 --> 00:04:20,400
That doesn't come from you.

59
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:26,080
I'm sorry...

60
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:31,240
I'm not in a state
to give anyone good love.

61
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:38,360
So what should we do now?

62
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:42,600
Should we end it here

63
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,520
and never meet again?

64
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,360
It's up to you.

65
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:03,760
Then, do you still want to be friends?

66
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:08,480
Of course I do.

67
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,040
But do you...

68
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,440
want to be friends with someone like me?

69
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,720
What does

70
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:22,760
"someone like you" mean?

71
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:27,240
A worthless person

72
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:29,560
who is unemployed

73
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:32,360
and never felt like they fit in anywhere.

74
00:05:35,380 --> 00:05:37,720
It's like wearing a bra that's
the wrong size all the time?

75
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:42,720
Sometimes it feels empty,

76
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,660
but sometimes it's uncomfortable.

77
00:05:58,560 --> 00:05:59,440
Where are you going?

78
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:09,240
Sun, what are you doing?

79
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:14,560
If you can't pick the right bra,
then let me help you.

80
00:06:19,360 --> 00:06:21,360
You have to find the right size.

81
00:06:23,660 --> 00:06:26,000
Explore what you can do.

82
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,680
I don't think

83
00:06:29,120 --> 00:06:30,380
you're worthless.

84
00:06:32,700 --> 00:06:34,640
You were just in the wrong place.

85
00:06:40,760 --> 00:06:43,200
You have to choose a bra
that suits your breast shape.

86
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,400
If you know what your strong suit is,

87
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:49,360
you'll know where you should be.

88
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:56,760
Lastly... try it out first.

89
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,920
If you feel uncomfortable,

90
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:06,600
it's okay to run away.

91
00:07:08,060 --> 00:07:10,000
If the bra really is bad,

92
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:12,080
maybe...

93
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:15,140
it's better to discard it.

94
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:18,000
Mm.

95
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,280
I understand now.

96
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:21,920
I don't know

97
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:24,200
when I'll find a bra that fits.

98
00:07:29,920 --> 00:07:31,640
But your necklace

99
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,880
never felt uncomfortable.

100
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,800
I really want to be your friend.

101
00:07:40,600 --> 00:07:42,840
Because you pity someone
who can't choose her own bra?

102
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:44,800
No.

103
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:47,960
It's because you were willing to listen

104
00:07:48,280 --> 00:07:49,640
to what I was saying.

105
00:07:51,640 --> 00:07:54,140
Even though you didn't have to do that.

106
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:58,760
You make the person you're with feel seen

107
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,720
and acknowledged.

108
00:08:01,760 --> 00:08:02,560
That's the reason

109
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:04,760
I want to be your friend.

110
00:08:15,260 --> 00:08:17,000
Will you run tomorrow?

111
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,360
I don't know.

112
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:19,680
I don't want to promise anything.

113
00:08:21,680 --> 00:08:23,280
How about... the day after tomorrow?

114
00:08:25,960 --> 00:08:27,140
I don't know.

115
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,240
It depends if I have work or not.

116
00:08:31,520 --> 00:08:32,520
Okay.

117
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,700
I'll get going now.

118
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,680
Um, Chris?

119
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:50,400
Can I have your phone?

120
00:08:56,080 --> 00:08:57,040
Here.

121
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,720
If you want to know
if I'm running tomorrow,

122
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:15,840
you can call me.

123
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,760
Okay.

124
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,020
Your "okay" this time

125
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,600
sounds much more cheerful than earlier.

126
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:26,520
Next time, if you want something,
just tell me.

127
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:28,320
We're friends now.

128
00:09:28,900 --> 00:09:30,240
We can talk about anything.

129
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:32,800
Do you understand, friend?

130
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:38,040
Yes, friend.

131
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:50,640
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

132
00:09:59,620 --> 00:10:00,320
Nadear,

133
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,600
why did we co-own this restaurant?

134
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:06,400
You've asked me before, haven't you?

135
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:09,140
Are you annoyed

136
00:10:09,160 --> 00:10:11,320
that you've had to answer
the same question for years?

137
00:10:13,660 --> 00:10:15,960
I'm glad you care, actually.

138
00:10:17,360 --> 00:10:19,120
It makes me feel hopeful.

139
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:23,620
We opened this restaurant together

140
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:25,800
because

141
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:29,640
you've wanted to have your own business
since you were a student.

142
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:31,960
After we graduated,

143
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,740
Nan asked if we wanted
to open a restaurant,

144
00:10:33,760 --> 00:10:35,520
so the three of us
decided to invest together.

145
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,360
Were the three of us rich?

146
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:45,200
We borrowed money from
our parents to invest.

147
00:10:45,880 --> 00:10:47,160
It was very risky,

148
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:49,300
but it worked out.

149
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:52,800
We already paid our parents back in full.

150
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,880
Before you got hurt,

151
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:00,840
our restaurant was very profitable.

152
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:06,040
Does that mean it's not as profitable now?

153
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:08,160
Why?

154
00:11:08,800 --> 00:11:10,320
Is there a problem?

155
00:11:14,140 --> 00:11:16,240
Just the usual problems, Chris.

156
00:11:16,660 --> 00:11:18,480
The economy is bad,

157
00:11:19,240 --> 00:11:21,280
so people don't eat out as much.

158
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:25,120
But I've seen that we have
a lot of customers every day.

159
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:28,040
You weren't here when
we had no customers.

160
00:11:31,560 --> 00:11:32,320
Alright,

161
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:35,000
then I'll come to our restaurant every day.

162
00:11:36,400 --> 00:11:37,440
You don't have to do that.

163
00:11:38,520 --> 00:11:40,320
You're still recovering,

164
00:11:40,880 --> 00:11:42,520
so I don't want you to be stressed.

165
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:44,340
But I want to help...

166
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:46,000
I got this,

167
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:49,660
but I want to focus on work for now.

168
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:51,320
Let's talk later, alright, Chris?

169
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,020
Nan,

170
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:13,960
- Hm?
- can I talk to you about our restaurant?

171
00:12:14,800 --> 00:12:15,680
What do you want to know?

172
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,200
I can't remember anything,

173
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:19,720
so can you start from the beginning?

174
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:21,260
Whoa, that was years ago.

175
00:12:21,280 --> 00:12:22,480
Why do you want to know now?

176
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:24,320
Of course I want to know.

177
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:25,760
Just tell me.

178
00:12:27,760 --> 00:12:30,600
It started when we went
to a party together.

179
00:12:30,620 --> 00:12:33,200
I... was Nadear's senior buddy.

180
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:35,600
Mm, I know that.

181
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:38,500
I told her...

182
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:40,000
I want to open my own restaurant.

183
00:12:40,100 --> 00:12:42,280
You and Nadear were interested,
so we started it together.

184
00:12:42,800 --> 00:12:44,800
It was going to fail at first, because...

185
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:47,280
we couldn't find a good spot
at a reasonable price.

186
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:49,740
Until you told me to rent this place.

187
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:52,740
I didn't know that.

188
00:12:52,760 --> 00:12:54,280
Nadear never told me about this.

189
00:12:55,940 --> 00:12:57,360
You told me

190
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:59,560
your friend recommended this spot.

191
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,000
Which friend?

192
00:13:02,520 --> 00:13:05,760
I don't know. Ask your girlfriend.
Maybe she knows.

193
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:09,080
Can I talk to her in private?

194
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:12,120
Of course.

195
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:23,640
Can you stop asking others
about our restaurant?

196
00:13:24,280 --> 00:13:25,680
It doesn't sit well with me.

197
00:13:26,440 --> 00:13:29,000
It looks like you don't know
anything about our restaurant.

198
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:33,280
Well, I don't know anything because
you never have time to tell me anything.

199
00:13:34,860 --> 00:13:36,220
If I'm free,

200
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,040
I'll gladly tell you about it.

201
00:13:38,270 --> 00:13:40,880
Why wouldn't I want you
to know more about our restaurant?

202
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:43,520
I'm busy,

203
00:13:43,950 --> 00:13:46,080
and you're not well.

204
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,280
I want you to gradually
remember everything,

205
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:53,060
or maybe wait for me to tell you,

206
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:54,880
instead of learning things
by asking other people.

207
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:57,480
Then does that mean if I can't remember,

208
00:13:57,680 --> 00:13:59,840
I don't have the right to
know anything about our restaurant?

209
00:14:01,860 --> 00:14:03,680
I don't want to be like this forever.

210
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:04,960
I want to be normal.

211
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,280
I want to know what I did in the past.

212
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:08,800
I want to know everything.

213
00:14:08,980 --> 00:14:12,160
I don't want to keep trying to
remember things, but nothing comes to mind.

214
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,720
Don't you get it?

215
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:20,960
Okay, Chris,

216
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:24,840
from now on,

217
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:27,280
I'll answer all of your questions.

218
00:14:30,900 --> 00:14:33,200
Then... which one of my friends
told us to rent this place?

219
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:40,960
Chris suddenly became
interested in our restaurant.

220
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:43,120
She asked me so many questions.

221
00:14:43,980 --> 00:14:46,680
Doesn't that mean
Chris is interested in you?

222
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,400
No.

223
00:14:52,060 --> 00:14:55,000
It means Chris is trying to be independent.

224
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,120
She doesn't want to depend on me.

225
00:15:02,680 --> 00:15:04,240
What did you make of that?

226
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:07,300
She's practically trying
to break up with me.

227
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:14,640
You're overthinking it.

228
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:16,840
Chris is perfectly fine.

229
00:15:17,240 --> 00:15:19,680
She thought I cared about her again,

230
00:15:20,480 --> 00:15:23,000
but I really don't feel
anything towards her anymore.

231
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,880
I'm just trying to live my life.

232
00:15:28,460 --> 00:15:30,640
Is this what you call
giving her false hope?

233
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:35,000
How can you stop someone from hoping?

234
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:38,880
Follow your heart.

235
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,480
If you don't feel anything,

236
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,120
then show her that you don't.

237
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:47,600
Nadear will definitely understand.

238
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,520
I don't want to upset her.

239
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,680
Then are you upset

240
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:59,080
that you didn't get to
live the way you wanted?

241
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:02,120
If you still hold each other back,

242
00:16:03,860 --> 00:16:05,520
no one is going to be happy.

243
00:16:08,420 --> 00:16:09,420
Right?

244
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:22,860
As a doctor,

245
00:16:23,230 --> 00:16:25,280
what do you think?

246
00:16:27,080 --> 00:16:28,320
It's a good sign.

247
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:31,560
She's trying to get into your world.

248
00:16:35,720 --> 00:16:36,720
Really?

249
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:39,480
Yes.

250
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,440
If there's something off,

251
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:45,160
you'll be the first to know.

252
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:22,120
Can you stop asking others
about our restaurant?

253
00:17:22,440 --> 00:17:24,680
Then... which one of my friends
told us to rent this place?

254
00:17:25,120 --> 00:17:26,480
I forgot.

255
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:28,960
If I can remember, I'll tell you.

256
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:33,400
Let's discuss what you want to know later.

257
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,640
You make the person you're with feel seen

258
00:17:39,240 --> 00:17:40,720
and acknowledged.

259
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:42,440
That's the reason

260
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:44,680
I want to be your friend.

261
00:17:48,360 --> 00:17:50,080
Chris, you have to understand.

262
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:52,800
I have important things
to deal with right now.

263
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:10,240
I just saw your call.

264
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:12,060
If you're asking me to go running,

265
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:13,320
I'll have to decline.

266
00:18:14,360 --> 00:18:15,360
Sun...

267
00:18:16,240 --> 00:18:17,900
can I come to your room?

268
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:34,000
Tell me why you wanted to
talk to me this early.

269
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,640
I... want to talk to you.

270
00:18:43,180 --> 00:18:43,920
Alright,

271
00:18:44,360 --> 00:18:45,600
but let's not stand while we talk.

272
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:55,620
When it's early like this...

273
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,640
I don't want to deal with gravity yet.

274
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:00,720
You can get straight to the point.

275
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:09,080
I want to ask you something.

276
00:19:22,780 --> 00:19:25,200
Make some eye contact
when you talk, friend.

277
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:31,240
So,

278
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,680
what would you like to talk about?

279
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:38,230
[Third Person]

280
00:19:40,630 --> 00:19:43,230
[Third Person]

281
00:19:43,390 --> 00:19:45,670
So, what would you
like to talk about?

282
00:19:47,270 --> 00:19:48,590
Why don't you say anything?

283
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:51,830
Or...

284
00:19:52,470 --> 00:19:53,910
you want to do something else first?

285
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:01,870
I want to do something else first.

286
00:20:08,270 --> 00:20:09,310
Ooh!

287
00:20:10,930 --> 00:20:12,550
Gay panic, huh?

288
00:20:14,590 --> 00:20:15,750
Tease me however you want.

289
00:20:16,190 --> 00:20:17,650
Alright, I'm ready.

290
00:20:25,550 --> 00:20:27,950
Sun... don't do this.

291
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:30,110
I'm trying to hold myself back.

292
00:20:35,590 --> 00:20:37,710
Then when will you stop holding back?

293
00:20:38,470 --> 00:20:39,570
Sun...

294
00:20:45,930 --> 00:20:47,270
I'll stop.

295
00:20:49,450 --> 00:20:51,210
So, what do you want to talk about?

296
00:20:51,230 --> 00:20:52,150
Go ahead.

297
00:20:59,690 --> 00:21:00,630
Well...

298
00:21:01,070 --> 00:21:02,390
What would you do

299
00:21:03,100 --> 00:21:04,150
if you had a friend

300
00:21:04,170 --> 00:21:06,790
who wouldn't discuss
anything important in your life

301
00:21:08,830 --> 00:21:11,410
because she always had
other important things to do?

302
00:21:13,670 --> 00:21:14,590
Your girlfriend?

303
00:21:18,950 --> 00:21:21,110
If she won't discuss it with you,

304
00:21:21,430 --> 00:21:23,030
you'll have to make her realize

305
00:21:23,050 --> 00:21:24,190
you're important.

306
00:21:29,710 --> 00:21:31,710
[Third Person
Bar - Bistro]

307
00:21:38,830 --> 00:21:40,670
If she won't discuss it with you,

308
00:21:40,930 --> 00:21:42,550
you'll have to get her attention.

309
00:21:43,350 --> 00:21:44,390
How?

310
00:21:44,630 --> 00:21:45,790
I'll show you.

311
00:21:46,070 --> 00:21:48,030
You'll play someone who's strong-willed.

312
00:21:48,830 --> 00:21:49,710
Easy.

313
00:21:49,950 --> 00:21:51,370
I'm very strong-willed.

314
00:21:51,390 --> 00:21:53,070
You won't sway me.

315
00:22:05,710 --> 00:22:07,710
See? I don't feel anything.

316
00:22:08,250 --> 00:22:09,190
Hey,

317
00:22:09,810 --> 00:22:11,190
that's no fun.

318
00:22:18,950 --> 00:22:19,750
Sun!

319
00:22:20,970 --> 00:22:21,830
Sun.

320
00:22:23,510 --> 00:22:24,630
Are you alright?

321
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:26,870
Success!

322
00:22:28,130 --> 00:22:30,150
Oh, so you tricked me?

323
00:22:31,150 --> 00:22:33,030
Would I even get your attention otherwise?

324
00:22:34,150 --> 00:22:36,790
Why don't you do what your friend
wants you to do?

325
00:22:37,830 --> 00:22:39,310
Maybe she'll drop everything

326
00:22:39,330 --> 00:22:40,750
and take an interest in you.

327
00:22:53,990 --> 00:22:54,930
Leave it to me.

328
00:23:01,250 --> 00:23:02,270
What happened?

329
00:23:02,730 --> 00:23:04,330
I wanted to ask you that too.

330
00:23:04,350 --> 00:23:06,830
Chris suddenly swooped in
to serve that dish.

331
00:23:16,970 --> 00:23:17,750
Chris,

332
00:23:18,750 --> 00:23:19,830
what are you doing?

333
00:23:21,030 --> 00:23:22,430
I'm serving food.

334
00:23:22,790 --> 00:23:23,950
I'm serious.

335
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:26,510
Isn't this our restaurant?

336
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:27,950
I have to work, don't I?

337
00:23:32,630 --> 00:23:33,630
One moment, please.

338
00:23:37,430 --> 00:23:38,430
What would you like?

339
00:23:40,790 --> 00:23:42,390
What's gotten into her?

340
00:23:42,590 --> 00:23:43,590
She's enthusiastic.

341
00:23:44,790 --> 00:23:46,110
Has she recovered?

342
00:23:46,210 --> 00:23:47,790
That's why you let her work, right?

343
00:24:04,730 --> 00:24:06,730
One Wagyu green curry and soda set.

344
00:24:10,270 --> 00:24:11,830
Can we talk?

345
00:24:16,930 --> 00:24:18,930
Do I have to do something you don't like

346
00:24:19,190 --> 00:24:20,750
before you'll have time to talk to me?

347
00:24:22,190 --> 00:24:23,510
Are you going to stop me again?

348
00:24:24,470 --> 00:24:25,710
I'm not,

349
00:24:26,590 --> 00:24:28,830
but we already have a lot of waiters.

350
00:24:29,190 --> 00:24:30,470
If you want to work,

351
00:24:30,490 --> 00:24:32,390
go back to what you were doing.

352
00:24:34,010 --> 00:24:35,270
What I was doing?

353
00:24:36,250 --> 00:24:37,850
Behind-the-scenes stuff, marketing.

354
00:24:37,870 --> 00:24:40,030
Thinking of new ways to attract customers.

355
00:24:41,150 --> 00:24:42,990
If you can do it,

356
00:24:43,730 --> 00:24:45,630
you can come back to work as before.

357
00:24:54,430 --> 00:24:55,070
Let's go.

358
00:24:55,970 --> 00:24:57,710
- The movie was fun, yeah?
- Mm.

359
00:24:59,890 --> 00:25:01,210
I'll see you tomorrow.

360
00:25:01,230 --> 00:25:01,830
Okay.

361
00:25:01,970 --> 00:25:03,070
Drive home safe.

362
00:25:12,870 --> 00:25:13,670
Chris!

363
00:25:19,630 --> 00:25:20,870
When did you get here?

364
00:25:22,910 --> 00:25:25,350
I arrived just as you
came down with that woman.

365
00:25:26,270 --> 00:25:27,670
Why didn't you greet me then?

366
00:25:28,230 --> 00:25:29,150
That's Oil,

367
00:25:29,290 --> 00:25:30,270
my best friend.

368
00:25:31,150 --> 00:25:31,910
"Friend"?

369
00:25:32,830 --> 00:25:34,190
Mm, friend.

370
00:25:34,390 --> 00:25:35,590
Just like you.

371
00:25:43,330 --> 00:25:45,330
Did you come to see me about something?

372
00:25:48,550 --> 00:25:51,030
Congratulations, you got back to work.

373
00:25:52,130 --> 00:25:53,270
It's because of you.

374
00:25:53,750 --> 00:25:56,550
Without you,
I'd probably be living without a goal.

375
00:25:57,510 --> 00:25:59,430
You gave me a goal in life, too.

376
00:26:14,490 --> 00:26:15,310
One second.

377
00:26:23,510 --> 00:26:24,630
I bought you a sandwich.

378
00:26:24,790 --> 00:26:25,830
Thanks.

379
00:26:26,570 --> 00:26:28,050
In case you're hungry tonight.

380
00:26:29,790 --> 00:26:30,790
There's something in your hair.

381
00:26:34,270 --> 00:26:35,950
Go rest up. Good night.

382
00:26:36,470 --> 00:26:37,210
Bye.

383
00:26:37,230 --> 00:26:38,390
- See you.
- See you.

384
00:26:50,950 --> 00:26:51,750
Look.

385
00:26:52,830 --> 00:26:54,350
Isn't she extra?

386
00:26:54,590 --> 00:26:57,150
She still came back to get me
this sandwich after she left.

387
00:26:58,310 --> 00:27:01,230
She's probably worried I might
not have anything to eat

388
00:27:01,630 --> 00:27:03,510
because we have a date tomorrow morning.

389
00:27:06,190 --> 00:27:06,990
Date?

390
00:27:07,310 --> 00:27:07,990
Mm.

391
00:27:08,650 --> 00:27:09,870
A date to relieve some stress.

392
00:27:10,590 --> 00:27:11,950
Would you like to join us?

393
00:27:13,830 --> 00:27:14,870
Oil won't mind.

394
00:27:17,310 --> 00:27:19,470
It's okay, you guys go ahead.

395
00:27:34,750 --> 00:27:35,870
I changed my mind.

396
00:27:36,150 --> 00:27:37,390
May I join you?

397
00:27:45,030 --> 00:27:47,890
[Third Person]

398
00:27:50,290 --> 00:27:52,890
[Third Person]

399
00:27:55,450 --> 00:27:56,490
- Here are my papers.
- Thank you.

400
00:27:56,510 --> 00:27:57,810
- I'll be in your care.
- One moment, please.

401
00:27:58,770 --> 00:27:59,770
Oh, Sun.

402
00:28:03,510 --> 00:28:04,610
This is Oil.

403
00:28:04,710 --> 00:28:05,610
She's a doctor.

404
00:28:05,990 --> 00:28:07,030
We studied together,

405
00:28:07,290 --> 00:28:08,890
and she's also a shareholder in my clinic.

406
00:28:11,090 --> 00:28:12,570
Work is tough right now,

407
00:28:12,590 --> 00:28:15,050
so Oil invited me to take
a flower arrangement class.

408
00:28:15,210 --> 00:28:16,930
She told me it helps relieve stress.

409
00:28:19,130 --> 00:28:20,390
I'm Chris.

410
00:28:20,810 --> 00:28:22,290
Can I join you today?

411
00:28:22,970 --> 00:28:24,090
You don't need my permission.

412
00:28:24,650 --> 00:28:26,050
Anyone can take the class.

413
00:28:27,250 --> 00:28:28,610
Just sign up there.

414
00:28:33,610 --> 00:28:34,570
Shall we...

415
00:28:35,290 --> 00:28:36,690
go look at the flowers inside?

416
00:28:44,770 --> 00:28:45,490
Mm.

417
00:28:47,570 --> 00:28:49,250
Go ahead, I'll sign up first.

418
00:28:52,610 --> 00:28:54,210
Chris can take care of herself,

419
00:28:54,570 --> 00:28:55,330
right?

420
00:28:59,310 --> 00:29:00,210
Let's go.

421
00:29:10,050 --> 00:29:11,410
Alright, everyone,

422
00:29:11,430 --> 00:29:14,270
before we start arranging the flowers,

423
00:29:14,290 --> 00:29:15,810
I want you to picture

424
00:29:15,830 --> 00:29:17,430
who you want to give these flowers to

425
00:29:17,450 --> 00:29:18,730
and why.

426
00:29:18,930 --> 00:29:21,570
This way, the flowers
can truly fulfill their purpose.

427
00:29:24,770 --> 00:29:25,530
Sun,

428
00:29:28,330 --> 00:29:29,370
I'll...

429
00:29:29,930 --> 00:29:31,490
arrange these flowers for you.

430
00:29:33,010 --> 00:29:33,970
Fine,

431
00:29:34,150 --> 00:29:35,530
but if it's not beautiful, I don't want it.

432
00:29:36,330 --> 00:29:37,890
I'll shove it into your hands anyway.

433
00:29:40,810 --> 00:29:43,590
First, let's prepare the roses.

434
00:29:43,610 --> 00:29:45,510
Alright, everyone, look here.

435
00:29:45,530 --> 00:29:48,430
Pluck off any leaves

436
00:29:48,450 --> 00:29:50,390
that are below
where we'll tie them together.

437
00:29:50,410 --> 00:29:52,430
Take them all off to clear it up.

438
00:29:52,450 --> 00:29:53,910
Be careful of the thorns, too.

439
00:29:53,930 --> 00:29:55,270
Follow my steps.

440
00:29:55,290 --> 00:29:57,210
You can cut off the thorns.

441
00:30:02,970 --> 00:30:04,410
Hey, need help?

442
00:30:06,770 --> 00:30:08,050
Here, I'll help.

443
00:30:09,690 --> 00:30:10,770
Be careful of the thorns.

444
00:30:10,790 --> 00:30:11,570
You too.

445
00:30:21,930 --> 00:30:22,570
Ow!

446
00:30:33,370 --> 00:30:34,170
Um...

447
00:30:34,510 --> 00:30:36,090
I'll go treat it first.

448
00:30:55,650 --> 00:30:56,930
Can I help?

449
00:31:11,990 --> 00:31:14,050
Are you very close to Oil?

450
00:31:15,650 --> 00:31:17,050
Does it look that way?

451
00:31:19,710 --> 00:31:20,490
Yes...

452
00:31:26,450 --> 00:31:27,490
We're close.

453
00:31:28,370 --> 00:31:29,830
We studied together,

454
00:31:29,850 --> 00:31:31,250
worked together,

455
00:31:31,970 --> 00:31:34,210
went through good and bad things together.

456
00:31:36,530 --> 00:31:37,850
Without her,

457
00:31:37,950 --> 00:31:40,050
I wouldn't be here learning
about flower arrangement.

458
00:31:42,290 --> 00:31:45,450
She seems to be a very
important person for you.

459
00:31:49,250 --> 00:31:50,590
I admit

460
00:31:50,610 --> 00:31:51,930
that she's important to me.

461
00:31:56,170 --> 00:31:59,250
Am I intruding on your
date with someone important?

462
00:32:02,850 --> 00:32:03,850
Are you jealous?

463
00:32:12,190 --> 00:32:13,970
How can a friend be jealous of this?

464
00:32:14,530 --> 00:32:16,250
I just want to tell you that

465
00:32:17,570 --> 00:32:19,290
if we hadn't met,

466
00:32:22,010 --> 00:32:24,330
I wouldn't be taking
a flower arrangement class here either.

467
00:32:29,790 --> 00:32:31,250
Let's go back inside.

468
00:32:43,030 --> 00:32:44,950
Well done, everyone.

469
00:32:44,970 --> 00:32:46,570
But don't forget

470
00:32:46,590 --> 00:32:49,310
to let the flowers
you worked hard to arrange today

471
00:32:49,330 --> 00:32:51,010
fulfill their purpose.

472
00:33:04,970 --> 00:33:05,850
This is for you.

473
00:33:07,210 --> 00:33:08,810
I thought you were joking.

474
00:33:12,290 --> 00:33:13,770
Well, you know I'm serious.

475
00:33:18,150 --> 00:33:20,090
So, I'll go to the clinic after this.

476
00:33:20,570 --> 00:33:22,290
Wanna grab something to eat?

477
00:33:35,090 --> 00:33:36,290
I'm sorry.

478
00:33:36,550 --> 00:33:38,730
Maybe next time. I have to go.

479
00:33:38,970 --> 00:33:41,490
Can you take this to the clinic for me?

480
00:33:41,810 --> 00:33:43,050
I'll see you later.

481
00:33:44,050 --> 00:33:44,730
Mm.

482
00:34:06,710 --> 00:34:07,550
Chris!

483
00:34:07,570 --> 00:34:08,530
Wait for me!

484
00:34:13,130 --> 00:34:14,490
Sun, don't cross the road yet!

485
00:34:17,490 --> 00:34:18,610
What is it?!

486
00:34:30,590 --> 00:34:33,370
I haven't let my flowers
fulfill their purpose yet.

487
00:34:38,250 --> 00:34:39,370
Me too.

488
00:34:40,280 --> 00:34:42,170
I thought I wouldn't be able to give it to you.

489
00:34:43,290 --> 00:34:44,370
You have to.

490
00:34:44,770 --> 00:34:45,890
It's your goal, isn't it?

491
00:34:55,010 --> 00:34:55,930
So...

492
00:34:56,110 --> 00:34:57,730
why are you giving me your flowers?

493
00:35:00,110 --> 00:35:01,970
To celebrate our meeting.

494
00:35:02,530 --> 00:35:03,410
What about you?

495
00:35:04,070 --> 00:35:05,690
To say I'm glad I got to see you again.

496
00:36:05,890 --> 00:36:06,710
Wow.

497
00:36:06,730 --> 00:36:09,130
I was planning to treat you
to our first meal together,

498
00:36:09,610 --> 00:36:11,530
but you only wanted Pad Thai. That's it?

499
00:36:12,690 --> 00:36:13,570
Well, I like it.

500
00:36:14,770 --> 00:36:15,850
You do, too.

501
00:36:17,170 --> 00:36:18,490
Mm, that's true.

502
00:36:19,470 --> 00:36:20,470
How did you know that?

503
00:36:23,250 --> 00:36:24,810
- Your water.
- Thank you.

504
00:36:25,090 --> 00:36:26,150
What would you like today?

505
00:36:26,170 --> 00:36:28,370
Two Pad Thais and one fried
mussel pancake, no bean sprouts, please.

506
00:36:28,910 --> 00:36:29,450
Alright.

507
00:36:29,590 --> 00:36:30,610
Thank you.

508
00:36:34,490 --> 00:36:35,210
Hey...

509
00:36:35,850 --> 00:36:36,970
I'm sorry.

510
00:36:37,350 --> 00:36:40,490
I... ordered for you without asking first.

511
00:36:44,090 --> 00:36:45,250
No need to.

512
00:36:46,010 --> 00:36:47,490
You ordered correctly.

513
00:36:48,570 --> 00:36:49,610
How did you know

514
00:36:51,050 --> 00:36:52,570
that I don't like bean sprouts?

515
00:36:55,250 --> 00:36:56,250
I didn't.

516
00:36:56,970 --> 00:36:59,370
When I had to order the food,
I just said it without thinking.

517
00:37:03,990 --> 00:37:04,810
Why are you smiling?

518
00:37:06,930 --> 00:37:07,930
I'm happy.

519
00:37:08,490 --> 00:37:09,490
It's like...

520
00:37:09,510 --> 00:37:11,370
god is finally on my side.

521
00:37:16,010 --> 00:37:17,350
Thank you.

522
00:37:17,370 --> 00:37:18,210
Thank you.

523
00:37:19,730 --> 00:37:21,090
Hey, kids!

524
00:37:21,530 --> 00:37:23,370
What are you doing?
Fighting again, huh?!

525
00:37:25,110 --> 00:37:25,650
Oh!

526
00:37:26,710 --> 00:37:27,570
Come on!

527
00:37:27,890 --> 00:37:29,090
Go home!

528
00:37:29,770 --> 00:37:30,610
Hey...

529
00:37:31,130 --> 00:37:32,610
are the flowers okay?!

530
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:34,050
It's okay, Chris.

531
00:37:34,330 --> 00:37:35,290
It's okay.

532
00:37:36,450 --> 00:37:37,810
Will it get bruised?

533
00:37:38,810 --> 00:37:40,130
It's still pretty.

534
00:37:41,490 --> 00:37:43,850
Even if the flowers aren't in a bouquet,

535
00:37:44,250 --> 00:37:45,050
they're still pretty.

536
00:37:54,230 --> 00:37:54,930
This is it.

537
00:37:55,690 --> 00:37:57,290
This is something new
my restaurant needs.

538
00:38:01,890 --> 00:38:03,250
Thank you so much, Sun.

539
00:38:18,310 --> 00:38:20,370
Where've you been today, Chris?

540
00:38:24,710 --> 00:38:26,170
Nice flowers.

541
00:38:27,190 --> 00:38:28,490
Who gave them to you?

542
00:38:31,730 --> 00:38:32,930
It's mine.

543
00:38:33,410 --> 00:38:35,170
I took a flower arranging class.

544
00:38:37,090 --> 00:38:38,330
With who?

545
00:38:39,390 --> 00:38:40,130
My friend.

546
00:38:41,290 --> 00:38:42,730
Since when did you have a friend?

547
00:38:43,910 --> 00:38:45,270
We met when I was out running.

548
00:38:47,890 --> 00:38:49,890
You haven't told me this before.

549
00:38:51,010 --> 00:38:52,490
Introduce me to them.

550
00:38:52,690 --> 00:38:54,690
I want to get to know your friend, too.

551
00:38:57,870 --> 00:38:58,850
Okay...

552
00:39:06,930 --> 00:39:08,250
Where are you taking it?

553
00:39:11,530 --> 00:39:13,410
You're the same as always, huh?

554
00:39:19,510 --> 00:39:20,650
The same...?

555
00:39:23,590 --> 00:39:25,210
You like roses.

556
00:39:26,730 --> 00:39:27,970
When you were younger,

557
00:39:28,530 --> 00:39:31,730
you loved the rose I gave you so much.

558
00:39:35,070 --> 00:39:36,570
You don't remember, do you?

559
00:39:40,570 --> 00:39:42,090
But I'm glad

560
00:39:42,610 --> 00:39:44,530
that you chose these roses.

561
00:39:46,330 --> 00:39:48,450
It means deep down...

562
00:39:49,490 --> 00:39:51,370
you haven't forgotten me yet.

563
00:39:53,770 --> 00:39:55,610
You haven't forgotten about us.

564
00:40:08,410 --> 00:40:09,990
Just a bit longer...

565
00:40:13,030 --> 00:40:15,490
I miss the you from back then.

566
00:40:35,010 --> 00:40:38,530
I want the Chris I know back.

567
00:40:48,330 --> 00:40:49,050
Here.

568
00:40:50,570 --> 00:40:51,930
Did you buy these to give to people?

569
00:40:53,090 --> 00:40:53,970
No,

570
00:40:54,110 --> 00:40:55,370
they're offerings for Buddha.

571
00:40:56,330 --> 00:40:58,130
Then no thanks. I don't want to
take one meant for Buddha.

572
00:40:58,770 --> 00:41:00,530
This one isn't an offering.

573
00:41:01,290 --> 00:41:02,890
I want to give it to you.

574
00:41:24,690 --> 00:41:25,370
Wait!

575
00:41:49,210 --> 00:41:51,770
When are you going to stop flirting
with someone who already has a girlfriend?

576
00:41:53,450 --> 00:41:54,770
They already broke up.

577
00:41:55,010 --> 00:41:57,610
That's what everyone who wants
someone who's taken says.

578
00:41:58,090 --> 00:41:59,690
If she can't make their relationship public,

579
00:41:59,890 --> 00:42:00,930
don't play with her.

580
00:42:07,250 --> 00:42:09,170
I didn't start it.

581
00:42:10,290 --> 00:42:12,890
You saw how she felt about me, right?

582
00:42:12,910 --> 00:42:15,050
It doesn't matter how much she likes you.

583
00:42:15,730 --> 00:42:17,570
As long as she hasn't broken up
with her girlfriend

584
00:42:17,590 --> 00:42:19,010
and told you that you're just a friend,

585
00:42:20,050 --> 00:42:21,490
doesn't that mean
she doesn't choose you?

586
00:42:27,690 --> 00:42:30,710
[Third Person]

587
00:42:33,014 --> 00:42:35,714
[Third Person]

588
00:42:36,634 --> 00:42:38,834
I want to add edible flowers to our dishes.

589
00:42:38,934 --> 00:42:40,394
So that we have something new

590
00:42:40,454 --> 00:42:41,654
that's pretty,

591
00:42:41,674 --> 00:42:43,234
appetizing,

592
00:42:43,434 --> 00:42:44,754
and photogenic.

593
00:42:45,774 --> 00:42:47,214
I think it could attract more customers.

594
00:42:47,234 --> 00:42:48,274
What do you think?

595
00:42:49,454 --> 00:42:50,434
I agree.

596
00:43:00,634 --> 00:43:01,674
It's pretty interesting.

597
00:43:02,434 --> 00:43:03,694
Thanks, Nadear.

598
00:43:03,714 --> 00:43:04,954
Thanks, Nan.

599
00:43:12,134 --> 00:43:14,154
Something new? Flowers? Really?

600
00:43:15,254 --> 00:43:16,674
No other restaurants do this, yeah?

601
00:43:20,394 --> 00:43:21,514
How did you agree?

602
00:43:22,154 --> 00:43:23,874
Chris is a shareholder as well.

603
00:43:24,614 --> 00:43:25,714
I want Chris to do this.

604
00:43:26,034 --> 00:43:27,354
You say it's good, but is it good

605
00:43:27,414 --> 00:43:28,754
for our business?

606
00:43:28,994 --> 00:43:31,114
Or is it for the relationship between you two?

607
00:43:31,954 --> 00:43:33,834
Can you stop asking about
my personal life?

608
00:43:34,474 --> 00:43:35,954
Be more rational, Nadear.

609
00:43:36,794 --> 00:43:38,214
Do you really think

610
00:43:38,234 --> 00:43:39,954
these edible flowers

611
00:43:40,094 --> 00:43:41,234
won't be a waste of our budget?

612
00:43:41,514 --> 00:43:43,114
I insist on letting Chris do it.

613
00:43:43,634 --> 00:43:44,954
Even if it's bad,

614
00:43:44,974 --> 00:43:46,054
wasteful,

615
00:43:46,074 --> 00:43:47,014
not worthwhile,

616
00:43:47,034 --> 00:43:48,514
or a loss for us.

617
00:43:49,634 --> 00:43:50,994
Is that really okay?

618
00:43:51,434 --> 00:43:52,754
What are you thinking?

619
00:43:53,614 --> 00:43:54,754
Stop fighting.

620
00:44:00,434 --> 00:44:02,514
I'll make this flower dish worthwhile

621
00:44:02,994 --> 00:44:04,274
and profitable.

622
00:44:15,674 --> 00:44:17,874
I don't think your idea is bad.

623
00:44:18,094 --> 00:44:20,634
I just said that to get Nan to let you do it.

624
00:44:21,114 --> 00:44:23,034
I didn't want to upset you.

625
00:44:25,554 --> 00:44:27,274
When will you understand

626
00:44:28,094 --> 00:44:30,474
that I don't want you to protect me like this?

627
00:44:31,274 --> 00:44:32,914
I want sincerity.

628
00:44:34,254 --> 00:44:37,714
When will you stop treating me
like someone about to die?

629
00:44:38,474 --> 00:44:39,754
You wouldn't know

630
00:44:41,674 --> 00:44:43,554
how much pain I was in

631
00:44:45,114 --> 00:44:47,114
when you were dying.

632
00:44:48,574 --> 00:44:49,394
Chris!

633
00:44:49,734 --> 00:44:50,514
Chris!

634
00:44:54,274 --> 00:44:55,934
I don't want to see you in pain

635
00:44:55,954 --> 00:44:57,994
or see you sad anymore,

636
00:44:58,674 --> 00:45:00,634
because I love you!

637
00:45:01,474 --> 00:45:02,874
Am I wrong for that?

638
00:45:03,694 --> 00:45:06,114
I'm the one who loves you more.

639
00:45:09,974 --> 00:45:12,154
Am I that wrong?

640
00:45:26,414 --> 00:45:27,474
I'm sorry...

641
00:45:39,154 --> 00:45:41,154
You don't want me to feel sad

642
00:45:43,314 --> 00:45:45,234
because my idea was that terrible?

643
00:47:07,954 --> 00:47:09,594
Didn't you say
you wanted to be my friend?

644
00:47:10,314 --> 00:47:11,914
Why are you avoiding me?

645
00:47:18,794 --> 00:47:20,394
I can't bring myself to see you.

646
00:47:21,514 --> 00:47:22,634
I'm an awful person.

647
00:47:24,494 --> 00:47:26,234
There's no place where I fit.

648
00:47:27,794 --> 00:47:29,714
If it doesn't fit, then why
don't you throw it away?

649
00:47:33,714 --> 00:47:35,714
Because it used to be amazing, I guess?

650
00:47:37,254 --> 00:47:38,594
That's why I can't discard it...

651
00:47:39,574 --> 00:47:40,354
What?

652
00:47:41,954 --> 00:47:44,234
Then what about the flowers in the dish?

653
00:47:47,834 --> 00:47:50,394
It'd be better if I didn't do anything.

654
00:47:55,154 --> 00:47:55,874
Let's go.

655
00:47:58,214 --> 00:47:59,074
Where?

656
00:48:00,814 --> 00:48:03,234
Somewhere to make you stop
thinking you're awful.

657
00:48:17,494 --> 00:48:23,374
♫The umbrella we once used to share♫

658
00:48:23,394 --> 00:48:28,834
♫Two bodies leaning close beneath the rain♫

659
00:48:29,554 --> 00:48:35,674
♫I never felt cold in your warmth♫

660
00:48:35,714 --> 00:48:39,954
♫Because you were there every time♫

661
00:48:39,974 --> 00:48:41,234
Do I hold the light here?

662
00:48:41,794 --> 00:48:42,594
Yes.

663
00:48:43,234 --> 00:48:44,634
See? It came out beautifully.

664
00:48:48,734 --> 00:48:49,514
But...

665
00:48:50,574 --> 00:48:52,574
If we do this, won't it be a loss?

666
00:48:54,654 --> 00:48:56,674
You can make it profitable.

667
00:48:57,394 --> 00:48:58,354
Trust me.

668
00:48:59,134 --> 00:49:00,134
Give it a try,

669
00:49:01,214 --> 00:49:02,654
so you'll know

670
00:49:02,674 --> 00:49:04,274
you're not as awful as you think.

671
00:49:06,354 --> 00:49:12,714
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

672
00:49:12,734 --> 00:49:13,514
Whoa,

673
00:49:13,894 --> 00:49:16,834
The food cost for this
flower dish is thirty percent.

674
00:49:17,674 --> 00:49:19,334
Then that means...

675
00:49:19,354 --> 00:49:21,354
we have around seventy percent profit.

676
00:49:21,834 --> 00:49:24,914
I think it could work
after we subtract other expenses.

677
00:49:25,634 --> 00:49:30,694
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

678
00:49:30,714 --> 00:49:32,594
See? You're not awful.

679
00:49:34,114 --> 00:49:35,514
I'm good in theory.

680
00:49:35,794 --> 00:49:38,514
What if people don't buy it?

681
00:49:39,514 --> 00:49:40,354
Well...

682
00:49:40,754 --> 00:49:41,634
it's going to be sad.

683
00:49:42,394 --> 00:49:44,634
But isn't it sadder

684
00:49:44,914 --> 00:49:48,354
if you didn't do what you love,

685
00:49:49,434 --> 00:49:51,874
didn't follow your heart?

686
00:49:52,534 --> 00:49:54,474
Would life have any meaning that way?

687
00:49:58,194 --> 00:49:59,674
Thank you so much, Sun.

688
00:50:02,074 --> 00:50:03,194
Can I hug you?

689
00:50:19,314 --> 00:50:20,794
You can drop me off here.

690
00:50:21,074 --> 00:50:23,034
I can take you home.

691
00:50:26,654 --> 00:50:27,594
It's okay.

692
00:50:27,614 --> 00:50:29,154
I'll get there myself.

693
00:50:29,254 --> 00:50:30,874
You helped a lot already.

694
00:50:32,094 --> 00:50:33,914
It's my pleasure.

695
00:50:34,994 --> 00:50:36,594
If your car isn't fixed yet,

696
00:50:37,114 --> 00:50:38,354
you can call me.

697
00:50:38,634 --> 00:50:40,154
Your chauffeur is on standby.

698
00:50:40,834 --> 00:50:42,354
Thank you so much, Sun.

699
00:50:43,194 --> 00:50:45,154
I stopped feeling like
an awful person because of you.

700
00:50:46,314 --> 00:50:47,834
You're a "talented one" now, aren't you?

701
00:50:48,314 --> 00:50:49,234
Good job.

702
00:50:50,234 --> 00:50:51,714
Thank you, really.

703
00:51:03,354 --> 00:51:04,554
Are you kissing as thanks?

704
00:51:06,974 --> 00:51:07,794
Mm...

705
00:51:09,554 --> 00:51:11,434
Friends don't kiss, do they?

706
00:52:00,394 --> 00:52:01,234
I'll go now.

707
00:52:23,254 --> 00:52:25,954
We were never friends, Chris...

708
00:52:48,714 --> 00:52:49,914
I kissed you,

709
00:52:50,714 --> 00:52:52,554
because I don't want to be just friends.

710
00:52:52,994 --> 00:52:54,994
Even though I can't recall anything,

711
00:52:55,554 --> 00:52:57,454
my heart still flutters

712
00:52:57,474 --> 00:52:59,954
every time I see that smile.

713
00:53:01,154 --> 00:53:04,674
I won't let anyone come between us.

714
00:53:05,274 --> 00:53:07,814
Can you give me three months?

715
00:53:07,834 --> 00:53:10,694
Three months to go back
to how it used to be.

716
00:53:10,714 --> 00:53:13,794
I don't want to keep living like
this anymore, Nadear.

717
00:53:32,034 --> 00:53:41,914
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

718
00:53:41,934 --> 00:53:47,034
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

719
00:53:47,054 --> 00:53:50,934
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

720
00:53:51,214 --> 00:53:57,094
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

721
00:53:57,114 --> 00:54:06,894
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

722
00:54:06,914 --> 00:54:11,974
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

723
00:54:11,994 --> 00:54:16,254
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

724
00:54:16,274 --> 00:54:25,154
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫

725
00:54:25,554 --> 00:54:34,194
♫Before the last raindrop falls,
don't make me shed another tear♫
